== screenplay
FROM SEED TO SEEDLING  (30 s; 3 scenes, 4 shots)
synopsis: A red kidney bean sits partly planted in white granular perlite, its hard coat and hilum established in seven seconds of live-action macro photography. Eight seconds of simple animation compress days 1–8: the seed absorbs water and swells, the radicle emerges first, and roots and a shoot develop in opposite vertical directions. Live-action time-lapse then shows days 11–12 as two unifoliate leaves unfold and expand. The film ends on the paired-leaf seedling with its terminal apex exposed between the leaves.
theme: Quiet potential becomes visible through patient observation.
music: Minimal ambient instrumental, patient and gently hopeful, soft felt piano and warm sustained synthesizer, 72 bpm, no vocals or percussion.   arc: [0s] Begin with sparse, widely spaced piano notes.  [7s] Introduce a quiet sustained synthesizer layer beneath the narration.  [15s] Warm the harmony slightly as live-action time-lapse returns.  [28s] Resolve softly and sustain through the final held image, ending at second 30.

